WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.934
- I know obviously when the

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:04.404
Jordan Poole video came out, there was
a lot of chatter about that video.

00:00:04.838 --> 00:00:08.942
But when you watch that video,
how do you feel about yourself?

00:00:09.609 --> 00:00:12.712
- Well, when I watched the video—

00:00:12.712 --> 00:00:15.281
when that video first came out,
I watched that video...

00:00:16.216 --> 00:00:17.584
all day.

00:00:19.352 --> 00:00:21.154
Go to it. Watch it.

00:00:21.154 --> 00:00:24.157
Watch it over and over again.

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:25.759
Leave it. Go do something else.

00:00:25.759 --> 00:00:26.860
Come back to the video.

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:31.031
Watch it again.
Because that video had me form

00:00:31.031 --> 00:00:34.134
an opinion about myself.

00:00:34.134 --> 00:00:35.568
And I was sitting there,

00:00:35.568 --> 00:00:38.371
and as someone who was involved

00:00:38.538 --> 00:00:41.341
in the incident, I totally forgot

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:46.112
in watching the video
everything that went on.

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:49.382
Because in the video, you watch an audioless
video, you watch a three-

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:53.553
second clip of me walking up,
and I swing, and, like, that's what you see.

00:00:54.621 --> 00:00:57.223
That video was put out there like that
to portray me

00:00:57.257 --> 00:01:01.094
the exact way it did.

00:01:01.094 --> 00:01:03.630
Does that mean I was not wrong in
what I did?

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:07.367
No. That does not mean

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:10.203
that. One hundred percent was the wrong reaction.

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:11.137
- Mmhmm.

00:01:14.541 --> 00:01:15.842
- But in everything,

00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:19.345
there's also a full story.

00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:22.382
I don't care to share my story.

00:01:22.382 --> 00:01:24.184
One day I will.

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:26.152
It ain't the time nor the place,

00:01:26.152 --> 00:01:28.021
nor do I care to share it.

00:01:28.021 --> 00:01:30.390
Care more about figuring this team out
and trying to win.

00:01:31.391 --> 00:01:33.526
But one day I will cuz

00:01:33.526 --> 00:01:35.495
there's always a time.

00:01:36.463 --> 00:01:37.464
But what I

00:01:37.464 --> 00:01:41.634
figured out
in watching that video for all day is, like,

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:45.572
“Damn, this is,

00:01:45.572 --> 00:01:48.541
this actually was
what this was meant to do.” Like,

00:01:48.875 --> 00:01:51.578
this was meant to form an opinion about me

00:01:53.947 --> 00:01:55.982
and not give another side to it.

00:01:55.982 --> 00:01:59.052
Like, not even allow another opinion
to be formed.

00:01:59.085 --> 00:02:01.254
This video was put out just like this—

00:02:02.455 --> 00:02:05.925
no audio.

00:02:05.925 --> 00:02:09.129
If we've got this video,
we got the whole practice, right?

00:02:09.129 --> 00:02:11.131
Like, we got everything, right?
- Mmhmm.

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:14.434
- All you see is, what, five seconds?

00:02:15.902 --> 00:02:18.638
And so what I had to do is No. 1, and—

00:02:20.273 --> 00:02:24.711
because, like, once that released,
I'm experiencing so many emotions, right?

00:02:24.711 --> 00:02:26.112
Like, I'm upset.

00:02:26.112 --> 00:02:28.648
Like, how the hell does this get released?

00:02:29.482 --> 00:02:33.453
I'm, like,

00:02:33.453 --> 00:02:35.555
going through hell

00:02:37.724 --> 00:02:39.192
because you're,

00:02:39.192 --> 00:02:42.061
I mean,

00:02:42.061 --> 00:02:44.864
just at the sole discretion
of public opinion.

00:02:46.232 --> 00:02:53.406
And on the flip side of that,

00:02:53.406 --> 00:02:57.377
also dealing with my team,
whose sentiments

00:02:57.377 --> 00:03:00.446
also changed once the video came out.

00:03:00.446 --> 00:03:02.815
So, here you are, here I am

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:07.253
in a situation where

00:03:07.453 --> 00:03:09.656
everybody was there, everyone attended,

00:03:11.291 --> 00:03:13.526
whatever was gonna be was gonna be.

00:03:13.526 --> 00:03:17.430
And then the video comes out,
and everything changes.

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:19.666
And so now I'm like, “Wow.”

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:23.303
But that's what this was intended to do.

00:03:23.303 --> 00:03:26.806
That's why this was released this way.

00:03:26.806 --> 00:03:29.409
And so in going through every emotion

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:34.247
and experiencing
all the different emotions

00:03:34.247 --> 00:03:38.351
that I was experiencing, in order

00:03:38.351 --> 00:03:42.288
for me
to even start to unpack this whole thing,

00:03:43.022 --> 00:03:45.391
I have to look at it
from every point of view.

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:46.893
Like, I can't just go in like, “Well,

00:03:46.893 --> 00:03:48.695
this is the point of view

00:03:48.695 --> 00:03:51.931
I'm gonna look at it from and that’s it.”
Like, you come out very shortsighted.

00:03:51.931 --> 00:03:55.034
Like, you come out with
not all the facts. You come out with

00:03:56.102 --> 00:03:56.970
not a complete

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:59.105
understanding because you didn't
look at a complete picture.

00:04:00.073 --> 00:04:01.574
And so

00:04:03.343 --> 00:04:07.046
I had to start looking at this thing
from, like, so many different viewpoints

00:04:07.046 --> 00:04:09.749
and trusting different people’s viewpoints
that I trust, you know,

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:15.822
trusting some people’s viewpoints
that I don't trust, like, and just really using

00:04:15.822 --> 00:04:20.126
that to kind of dissect
and unpack this whole thing.

00:04:21.394 --> 00:04:23.396
And in doing

00:04:23.396 --> 00:04:29.302
that,
it really led me to some different spaces.

00:04:29.302 --> 00:04:31.471
But like I said, one of those spaces being

00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:36.509
this was put out like this

00:04:36.843 --> 00:04:40.213
to form that opinion on me
that it did.

00:04:40.446 --> 00:04:43.082
- So, just a clarifying question
cuz I'm curious.

00:04:43.082 --> 00:04:45.618
And I can't tell
if this is what you're really insinuating, and

00:04:45.652 --> 00:04:47.220
I don't want to be wrong.

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:49.922
The video coming out
you feel like was, like,

00:04:50.523 --> 00:04:53.926
a calculated thing
for the video to come out.
- One hundred percent.

00:04:55.061 --> 00:04:56.229
- OK.

00:04:56.229 --> 00:04:58.665
- You ain't never seen another video
from my practice

00:05:01.868 --> 00:05:04.737
That camera gotta
be on every day, right?

00:05:04.737 --> 00:05:06.873
Or was it just on that day, in that moment,

00:05:06.873 --> 00:05:10.710
for those five seconds?

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:12.845
You ain’t see one of our plays draw—

00:05:12.845 --> 00:05:16.683
that we drawn up in practice
coming out from those videos.

00:05:16.683 --> 00:05:22.021
You ain't seen anything else
coming out from practicing those videos.

00:05:22.021 --> 00:05:24.123
So, it's 100 percent calculated.

00:05:24.691 --> 00:05:26.492
Who was it calculated by?

00:05:26.492 --> 00:05:28.528
I don't know.
I would still love to know that answer.

00:05:28.594 --> 00:05:31.197
I still don't have an answer
on how the video got released.

00:05:32.899 --> 00:05:35.335
Not sure I will ever get an answer.

00:05:35.335 --> 00:05:37.603
To be honest with you,
I'm not even in search of an answer.

00:05:37.603 --> 00:05:41.274
I would love to know, but I ain't chasing
after it. For what? It's a waste of my time.

00:05:42.175 --> 00:05:43.409
What happened, happened.

00:05:44.844 --> 00:05:46.846
I accepted my responsibility in it.

00:05:46.846 --> 00:05:48.381
And once I accepted,

00:05:48.381 --> 00:05:52.151
once I accepted my responsibility,
then I started to move forward.

00:05:52.652 --> 00:05:55.755
- Mmhmm.
- Like, I accepted my responsibility. I knew I was wrong.

00:05:55.755 --> 00:05:59.692
I apologized to those
that I needed to apologize to.

00:05:59.692 --> 00:06:02.128
And now it's time to do the work
and move forward.

00:06:02.161 --> 00:06:05.998
And so, in saying that, I'm
not gonna spend a bunch of time going

00:06:06.032 --> 00:06:07.800
to try to figure out—
- Right.

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:10.503
- Who released it,
because it’s behind me, you know?

00:06:11.237 --> 00:06:13.072
And I want it to stay behind me.

00:06:13.072 --> 00:06:15.208
I don't wanna put that back
in front of me. And so, um,

00:06:17.276 --> 00:06:20.279
but it's 100 percent a calculated thing

00:06:20.279 --> 00:06:24.384
by whoever released it or
whoever was behind it. It’s 100 percent calculated.

00:06:24.717 --> 00:06:26.953
I wish I knew the answer of who

00:06:26.953 --> 00:06:30.022
it was calculated by.
- Mmhmm.
- But it's definitely calculated.

00:06:31.023 --> 00:06:32.658
- So, with you—and I knowobviously

00:06:32.658 --> 00:06:36.262
I’ve listened to your podcast talking about it.
I saw the piece you did on TNT and, like,

00:06:36.662 --> 00:06:40.800
taking the responsibility of being wrong
in the video. That what you did,

00:06:41.033 --> 00:06:44.337
you know, and I honestly
don't really know the question to ask

00:06:44.337 --> 00:06:46.205
because we don't know what happened,
you know?

00:06:46.205 --> 00:06:48.474
And that's not a thing you wanna share,
and that's totally fine.

00:06:49.175 --> 00:06:52.879
But with the information
that we have presented to us

00:06:52.879 --> 00:06:55.081
from what we saw in the video,

00:06:55.081 --> 00:06:58.951
do you think that you all have been able
to be in this space to move forward?

00:06:58.985 --> 00:07:03.656
Do you think that you have shown to Jordan,
based on what we have seen,

00:07:03.656 --> 00:07:09.061
that you are sorry, that you want to move
forward, that it can be put behind you?

00:07:09.662 --> 00:07:19.272
- Ah...

00:07:19.272 --> 00:07:22.942
We go to work every day together.

00:07:23.509 --> 00:07:26.012
Our lockers are right next to each other.

00:07:26.012 --> 00:07:27.046
That never changed.

00:07:28.648 --> 00:07:31.551
We ride the same buses together.

00:07:31.551 --> 00:07:36.422
We change in the same locker room
on the road together. We—

00:07:36.422 --> 00:07:39.459
none of that has changed.

00:07:39.459 --> 00:07:41.060
Did it change our relationship?

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:43.095
Of course! Absolutely.

00:07:44.764 --> 00:07:47.767
That's still a work in progress.

00:07:47.767 --> 00:07:50.236
I will always be willing to continue
to do that work

00:07:50.236 --> 00:07:59.212
because I was wrong.
- Mmhmm.

00:07:59.212 --> 00:08:02.048
- And so, in saying all of that,

00:08:02.048 --> 00:08:05.718
yes. Like,
definitely allowed to move forward.

00:08:05.852 --> 00:08:13.292
And we have moved forward,
and it's been just fine.

00:08:13.292 --> 00:08:17.563
But is it different? One hundred percent.

00:08:17.563 --> 00:08:21.167
And not that
I expected it to be the same, right?

00:08:21.167 --> 00:08:25.171
Like, if I had to say back then, like,

00:08:25.171 --> 00:08:28.441
“Oh, I think this would go like this,”
or, “I think it'll go like that,”

00:08:29.675 --> 00:08:32.044
I can't say it's went very different

00:08:32.345 --> 00:08:35.715
or it's been very far off from the way
I thought it would go.

00:08:36.148 --> 00:08:36.415
- Mmhmm.

00:08:38.551 --> 00:08:39.252
- I think it's been

00:08:39.252 --> 00:08:41.454
pretty close
to the way that I thought it would go.

00:08:43.022 --> 00:08:46.092
But as far as, like, us moving forward,

00:08:46.092 --> 00:08:48.794
we've definitely moved forward.

00:08:51.998 --> 00:08:58.471
And...and I see improvements

00:08:59.906 --> 00:09:02.241
day by day, week by week,
month by month,

00:09:02.241 --> 00:09:03.175
I see improvements.

00:09:03.175 --> 00:09:04.810
- That's good.
- And that's all you can ask for,

00:09:04.810 --> 00:09:05.645
you know?

00:09:06.445 --> 00:09:08.281
I don't expect him to come out
and be like, “Man,

00:09:08.281 --> 00:09:09.882
I wanna come hang with you
off the court!”

00:09:09.882 --> 00:09:12.818
And, like, I don’t expect that. Like, I'm
not, I'm not a fool.

00:09:12.852 --> 00:09:16.422
Like, I grew up in Saginaw,
Michigan. Like, I’ve been in fights before.

00:09:16.956 --> 00:09:20.192
Like, been in this situation before. I know how
you come out of those situations.

00:09:20.192 --> 00:09:20.793
Like,

00:09:21.961 --> 00:09:24.163
it's not what I expected.
- Mmhmm.

00:09:24.163 --> 00:09:26.899
- So, in saying

00:09:26.899 --> 00:09:32.838
that, it's
kinda what I expected it to be,

00:09:34.173 --> 00:09:34.607
but it's a

00:09:34.607 --> 00:09:37.977
constant work in progress
because it's very important

00:09:37.977 --> 00:09:40.813
to the makeup of our team,
to the success of our team.

00:09:41.781 --> 00:09:43.950
- Mmhmm.
- And so, I continue to do the work.

